WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:43.600
[Music]

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.620
[Narrator:] This is an average small town.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.780
Population about 10,000.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.180
Pleasant homes. Some industry.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.260
Main Street.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:03.840
One of the 10,000-odd inhabitants is Anne Wheeler, 14 years old

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.520
and a student at the local junior high.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.800
And this is Roger Cartwright.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:14.340
He too is 14 years old and goes to the same school Anne is attending.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.660
There are lots of things we could tell you about Anne and Roger:

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:20.600
where they live, who their parents are,

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.940
what subjects they like at school.

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:27.200
But one thing we don't have to tell you; it's plain as day.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:34.400
Anne and Roger are healthy, sturdy, physically fit. Nothing very remarkable about that.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:39.960
For most young people these days, good health is something to be almost taken for granted.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:45.580
Well then, have you ever stopped to think why these young people, like most of us,

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.280
don't have to worry about their health?

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.720
Why is that so? Take this glass of water, for instance.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:57.000
What does a glass of water have to do with Anne's health?

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.660
It is quite simple, really.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:05.740
When water falls from the sky as rain, it may be pure and fit to drink,

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:08.180
but as it runs toward the sea,

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:13.120
water may become polluted because industrial wastes are discharged into it,

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.900
and also because of the wastes coming from [inaudible] cities.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:21.860
When a drop of such polluted water is observed under a microscope,

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:27.260
it can be seen that the water contains large concentrations of microorganisms,

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:33.020
which can cause disease like typhoid fever, dysentery, cholera, for example.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:38.420
Such microorganisms must be removed before we can safely drink the water.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:45.760
In America, even small communities are assured of clean, healthy drinking water,

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.220
whether their water needs purification,

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:52.180
or whether it is pure to begin with and has not been contaminated.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:56.460
The health department keeps a close watch over the supply to make sure

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:00.940
that only water that is safe to drink reaches the people of the community.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:10.080
And just like water, food too can carry dangerous disease-producing organisms.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.760
Therefore, to safeguard all members of the community against the many diseases

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.520
which can be spread by unclean food,

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.080
your local health department is concerned

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:24.280
with the purity of the many foods consumed by the people each day.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:31.420
Rigorous standards of cleanliness are established for all places where food is processed and handled.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:39.400
Everywhere the standards of cleanliness are enforced by frequent inspections.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:46.320
To further safeguard the health of a community, proper disposal of garbage is essential.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.520
If garbage is not properly disposed of,

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:55.640
disease organisms from the exposed garbage may be spread to food products

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:57.720
in homes or restaurants.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:03.400
Improper disposal of sewage may also endanger the health of the community.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:06.640
Rivers and streams may become polluted.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:11.920
Swimming holes and beaches may be ruined for recreation because sewage is discharged

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:16.460
into the waters of the community. Such hazards must be eliminated.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:19.660
Along with these responsibilities,

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:27.200
the local health department attempts in still other ways to prevent or limit the spread of communicable diseases.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:34.580
Scientists in the health department help to identify individual cases of the various communicable diseases

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:39.800
by making laboratory tests at the request of local physicians,

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:44.460
and whenever it is necessary, the local health department will supply vaccines

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:48.680
and other immunizing agents to physicians and hospitals.

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:52.920
Today, most physicians vaccinate infants and small children

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:57.220
against smallpox, diphtheria, whooping cough, tetanus,

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:02.940
and other common diseases for which immunizing agents have been developed.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:08.380
And school nurses, who are usually public health nurses working closely with the local health department,

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.440
keep careful watch on the health of students.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:17.340
Health education is another important function of a local health department.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:21.160
Pamphlets covering many aspects of achieving and maintaining good health

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:25.880
for all age groups are carefully planned and widely distributed.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:30.100
Well, all this and much more is part of the picture

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:35.760
of why, today, we have good reasons to take good health almost for granted.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:43.080
Anne and Roger can live in their community without too much danger from communicable diseases,

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:46.520
thanks largely to the work done by the local Department of Health,

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:51.140
but there are other agencies, the Red Cross, for example,

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:54.660
that supplement the work of the community health department.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:06:01.580
They are voluntary health organizations supported by contributions and frequently staffed by volunteers.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:05.380
Anne, as a volunteer in her local chapter of the Red Cross,

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:09.780
is helping to prepare emergency kits for use in a nearby disaster area,

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:12.060
one of the many jobs the Red Cross undertakes

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:15.100
to supplement the work of existing health agencies,

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.380
particularly in times of emergency.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:21.800
And then there are the many other voluntary health agencies

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:25.000
concerned with the problems of specific diseases.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:30.120
Some of these organizations are concerned with research,

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:36.480
others with rehabilitation and the tremendous burden of caring for the victims of the respective disease.

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:43.260
In many communities there are visiting nurse services

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:46.660
to provide home nursing care for bedridden patients.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.140
The larger urban centers frequently have a safety council

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:53.500
to guard against the many accident hazards

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:57.440
which occur on the roads, in industry, and in the home.

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:03.480
And now, together with Roger, we will come upon still another safeguard

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.280
which helps maintain the health of a community.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:09.300
Yes, the family doctor.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.840
Nothing wrong with Roger, as far as he knows.

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:17.960
This is just a periodic checkup, a routine examination, to make sure.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:26.160
Part of the job of a general practitioner is to treat his patients when they get sick,

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:30.720
but the community health part of his job is to prevent illness,

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:34.200
which is the chief purpose of periodic checkups.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:44.880
By examining Roger carefully, looking for any telltale signs that might indicate the possible onset of illness

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:47.520
or some condition that needs correcting,

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:52.480
the doctor is helping to keep Roger well and the community healthy.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:05.800
Family doctors like this one and all the other doctors,

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:10.800
the dentists, the specialists in the different branches of medicine,

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:17.520
the hospitals and clinics and the many laboratories that work with the doctors,

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:24.060
all are part of the network of people and organizations concerned with the health of the community.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:28.600
Yes, Roger and Anne are pretty healthy young people,

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:31.860
thanks in part to the work of the community health services,

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:35.540
but these services could not function so well

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:39.540
without the active cooperation of young people and their parents,

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:42.140
of all the other people who live in the community.

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:47.000
In practically every community,

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:51.220
we have important rules requiring us to observe habits of cleanliness.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:59.380
Good personal habits of cleanliness, besides helping to keep you healthy,

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:05.980
also reduce the chances of your infecting others with disease-bearing organisms which you may be carrying.

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:09.560
Also, everyone knows or should know

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:12.600
that bed is the best place for a cold,

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:15.180
because what seems to be nothing but a cold

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:19.100
may be the beginning of influenza or some other serious disease.

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.740
If you don't stay in bed,

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:25.980
you endanger not only your own health but also that of the other people in the community.

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:31.140
Roger and Anne understand the health problems of their community.

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:35.740
They, like the rest of us, must live by the rules of healthful living

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:41.100
for the sake of their own good health and for the health of their friends and neighbors.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.320
[Music]

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:49.640
Community health is a responsibility shared by all citizens, young and old alike.

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:53.340
[Music]

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:57.440
How much do you know about the health services in your community?

00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:02.080
What can you do to support or improve them?

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:27.220
[Music]

